    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\ns_nth = a/2 (2n - 1) and s_n = 1/2 a n\u00b2. Their ratio is (2n - 1) / n\u00b2 = 9/25.\n\n2. GIVEN:\ns_nth / s_n = 9 / 25.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\n(2n - 1) / n\u00b2 = 9 / 25\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Write the ratio: s_nth / s_n = [a/2 (2n - 1)] / [1/2 a n\u00b2] = (2n - 1) / n\u00b2.\n2. Set equal to 9/25: 25(2n - 1) = 9n\u00b2.\n3. 50n - 25 = 9n\u00b2 => 9n\u00b2 - 50n + 25 = 0.\n4. Factor: 9n\u00b2 - 45n - 5n + 25 = 0 => 9n(n - 5) - 5(n - 5) = 0 => (9n - 5)(n - 5) = 0.\n5. Since n must be an integer, n = 5.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption C: 5\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nVerify: For n = 5, 2n - 1 = 9 and n\u00b2 = 25, so ratio = 9/25 immediately!",
