    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nUse s_n = u + a/2 (2n - 1) for n = 2 and n = 4, then solve the system of two linear equations.\n\n2. GIVEN:\ns\u2082 = 12 m, s\u2084 = 20 m.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\ns_n = u + (a/2)(2n - 1)\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. For n = 2: 12 = u + (a/2)(2(2) - 1) = u + 1.5a  =>  u + 1.5a = 12.\n2. For n = 4: 20 = u + (a/2)(2(4) - 1) = u + 3.5a  =>  u + 3.5a = 20.\n3. Subtract equation 1 from equation 2: (3.5a - 1.5a) = 20 - 12 => 2a = 8 => a = 4 m/s\u00b2.\n4. Substitute a = 4 into equation 1: u + 1.5(4) = 12 => u + 6 = 12 => u = 6 m/s.\n5. Therefore, u = 6 m/s and a = 4 m/s\u00b2.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption B: u = 6 m/s, a = 4 m/s\u00b2\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nQuick shortcut: s_n\u2082 - s_n\u2081 = a (n\u2082 - n\u2081). Here 20 - 12 = a (4 - 2) => 8 = 2a => a = 4 m/s\u00b2 directly!",
