    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nThe speed at the midpoint of distance under constant acceleration is v_mid = \u221a[(u\u00b2 + v\u00b2)/2].\n\n2. GIVEN:\nu = 10 m/s, v = 30 m/s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv_mid = \u221a[(u\u00b2 + v\u00b2) / 2]\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Apply midpoint speed formula: v_mid = \u221a[(u\u00b2 + v\u00b2) / 2].\n2. u\u00b2 = 10\u00b2 = 100, and v\u00b2 = 30\u00b2 = 900.\n3. u\u00b2 + v\u00b2 = 100 + 900 = 1000.\n4. (u\u00b2 + v\u00b2) / 2 = 1000 / 2 = 500.\n5. v_mid = \u221a500 = \u221a(100 \u00d7 5) = 10\u221a5 m/s (\u2248 22.36 m/s).\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption B: 10\u221a5 m/s\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nNEET Trap: 20 m/s is the speed at the halfway TIME (10+30)/2 = 20 m/s. But halfway DISTANCE is 10\u221a5 m/s!",
