    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nConservation of mechanical energy: speed at any given height h is \u221a(u\u00b2 - 2gh) both going up and coming down. Magnitudes are identical, directions are opposite.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nSame height h on upward and downward paths.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv\u00b2 = u\u00b2 - 2gh => |v_up| = |v_down| = \u221a(u\u00b2 - 2gh)\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. By conservation of mechanical energy, potential energy at height h is the same (mgh).\n2. Therefore, kinetic energy is the same: 1/2 m v\u00b2 = 1/2 m u\u00b2 - mgh.\n3. Hence, the magnitude of velocity is identical: |v_up| = |v_down| = \u221a(u\u00b2 - 2gh).\n4. Upward velocity is +v, downward velocity is -v.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 1 : 1 in magnitude, opposite in direction\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nSymmetry of vertical flight: Speed at any level is the same going up as coming down!",
