    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nFor ball 1: -h = ut\u2081 - 1/2 gt\u2081\u00b2. For ball 2: -h = -ut\u2082 - 1/2 gt\u2082\u00b2. Eliminating u gives h = 1/2 g t\u2081 t\u2082. For dropped ball: h = 1/2 g t\u00b2. Equating gives t = \u221a(t\u2081 t\u2082).\n\n2. GIVEN:\nTimes t\u2081 (thrown up), t\u2082 (thrown down), t (dropped).\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nt = \u221a(t\u2081 t\u2082)\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Ball thrown upwards: -h = u t\u2081 - (1/2) g t\u2081\u00b2 => u t\u2081 = (1/2) g t\u2081\u00b2 - h.\n2. Ball thrown downwards: -h = -u t\u2082 - (1/2) g t\u2082\u00b2 => u t\u2082 = h - (1/2) g t\u2082\u00b2.\n3. Dividing equations: t\u2081 / t\u2082 = [(1/2) g t\u2081\u00b2 - h] / [h - (1/2) g t\u2082\u00b2].\n4. Cross multiplying and simplifying yields: h = (1/2) g t\u2081 t\u2082.\n5. For a ball dropped from rest: h = (1/2) g t\u00b2.\n6. Comparing both: (1/2) g t\u00b2 = (1/2) g t\u2081 t\u2082 => t\u00b2 = t\u2081 t\u2082 => t = \u221a(t\u2081 t\u2082).\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: t = \u221a(t\u2081 t\u2082)\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nFAMOUS NEET RESULT: Geometric mean of flight times! t = \u221a(t\u2081 t\u2082).",
