    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nTime of flight for each ball T = 2 \u221a(2h/g) = 2 \u221a(40/10) = 4 s. With 4 balls in the air, interval between throws is \u0394t = T / n = 4 / 4 = 1.0 s.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nHeight h = 20 m, number of balls n = 4, g = 10 m/s\u00b2.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nT = 2 \u221a(2h / g); \u0394t = T / n\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Time of flight for one ball: T = 2 \u221a(2h / g) = 2 \u221a(2 \u00d7 20 / 10) = 2 \u221a4 = 4 s.\n2. To keep 4 balls in the air continuously, the total time T must be divided equally among the 4 balls.\n3. Interval between successive throws: \u0394t = T / 4 = 4 s / 4 = 1.0 s.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 1.0 s\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nJuggling formula: Time interval between throws = (Time of flight of one ball) / (Number of balls).",
